 "script": "That suspected Amelia Earhart wreck in a Pacific lagoon was likely trees. Purdue University announced the result after a seventeen-person team spent four days on Nikumaroro. The shape was first spotted in satellite images in twenty-twenty. It even appeared in aerial photos from nineteen thirty-eight. But by the time the team arrived, much of it had washed away. Here's what they did find: a steel tube, about thirty inches long. Earhart vanished in nineteen thirty-seven. Purdue says the search goes on. Where do you think her plane ended up? Tell us below.",
